ure: Banking Regulation in the 21st Century, page 221:"}, {"text": "The wedding of black brass bands and orchestras to jubilee concert companies was a consolidation that favored both promoters and musicians.", "reference": "2002, Lynn Abbott, Doug Seroff, Out of Sight: The Rise of African American Popular Music, 1889-1895, page 176:"}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [{"language": {"code": "bg", "name": "Bulgarian"}, "word": "съчетаване"}, {"language": {"code": "bg", "name": "Bulgarian"}, "word": "съединяване"}, {"language": {"code": "fi", "name": "Finnish"}, "word": "yhdistäminen"}, {"language": {"code": "fi", "name": "Finnish"}, "word": "liitos"}, {"language": {"code": "fi", "name": "Finnish"}, "word": "liittäminen"}, {"language": {"code": "de", "name": "German"}, "word": "Hochzeit"}, {"language": {"code": "pl", "name": "Polish"}, "word": "poślubienie"}], "subsenses": []}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": []}, {"language": {"code": "en", "name": "English"}, "partOfSpeech": "verb", "pronunciations": [{"type": "ipa", "text": "/ˈwɛdɪŋ/", "tags": []}], "forms": [], "senses": [{"definition": "present participle and gerund of wed", "tags": ["form of", "gerund", "participle", "present"], "examples": [], "quotes": [{"text": "Accordingly the Prince, accepting her largesse, sought the King to whom he had pledged his parents (and they were still with him in all weal and welfare) and going in to him made his salam and kissed ground and told him the whole tale of the past and the conditions of death or marriage he had made with the King's daughter and of his wedding her after overcoming her in contention.", "reference": "1885, Richard Francis Burton, The Book of the Thousand Nights and a Night, volume 14:"}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": []}, {"language": {"code": "en", "name": "English"}, "partOfSpeech": "verb", "pronunciations": [{"type": "ipa", "text": "/ˈwɛdɪŋ/", "tags": []}], "forms": [{"wo